    "summary": "Compact slice sea: 111 x 111 tiles generated from a mirrored ASCII quarter (assets/source/maps/sketch.ts -> slice-sea.tmj, 24 px Tiled tiles, new `hub` point object) via the unchanged map:build pipeline. Four islands, reefs, and midline shoal walls that open only inside the hub's disc. Report: neighbours 26.4 s, longest crossing 39.3 s, first dock <= 7.3 s, largest obstacle distance 9.9 tiles, 90.7% open sea. New validators (density: every navigable tile within SIGHT_RADIUS_TILES of land/shoal/dock, squared integers, edge not counted; hub: open sea near the centre, closing the disc of radius SIGHT/2 must raise or cut the shortest cost for every cross-island dock pair), each shown failing on a synthetic map in maps.test.ts; map:build prints the largest obstacle distance, open-sea share and each route's closest approach to the hub. Tuning: maxSpeed 39, acceleration 3, braking 3, drag 1, maxReverseSpeed 10, reverseAcceleration 1, dockMaxSpeed 15, dockRadius 384, turnRate 1; simulation tests measure time to full speed, braking distance, full turn and turning circle in px against the old tuning at 16 px (all within 25%), plus a docking sweep (headings 46/47, x every 16 sub-units across 3 tiles east of the dock, 2-4 tiles out, two start speeds) that always moors. Web: TILE_PIXELS 24 (content constant shared by Tiled and the client), art scaled, minimap 1.25 px/tile; sea keyboard latches a tap of E until the next read (unit test shows it docks). Protocol test-placement schema is now built from the map's size (createTestPlacementSchema). All test positions come from the map (hub row) and are checked for a clear hull line. sail-and-dock now docks into the shore corner at heading 46/47 with ahead+E held; sailTo sails in hops (turn at rest, hold ahead for a computed number of steps, coast) so it is robust to HUD lag. Checks run here: npm ci; npm run typecheck (pass); npm run test:unit (548 pass); npm run test:integration (37 pass); npm run build incl. smoke (pass); full Playwright suite with JSON reporter, 6 passed, check-report OK; tests/e2e/sea.spec.ts --repeat-each=5: 10/10 passed (sail-and-dock 5 in a row) at load average 6-8.",
